"/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/1","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/10"],"concerns":["Inspect daemon embedding ownership, caller-supplied standalone vectors, SDK-to-native-binding relationships and compatibility with actual package and store implementations.","Assess reproducibility and delivery of the narrowed LanceDB distribution, including pinned provenance, checksum, licensing, optional provider removal and native target availability.","Verify that default packed-consumer installation is qualified independently of producer overrides, with every resolved advisory copy checked.","Assess Node 22.22.1 macOS and Linux native installation, ONNX startup, pre-upgrade store reopen, data preservation and rollback requirements.","Inspect historical snapshot preservation, low-alert exclusions, GitHub reconciliation, targeted batches and final repository sweep against originating ISSUE scope.","Inspect necessary relationship and packaging diagrams or definitions and actual renderings where available."],"dependsOn":["daemon","drivers"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Whole-design traceability and cross-chunk consistency","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile every originating ISSUE requirement with the complete LLD, including three reviewable batches, acceptance mappings, preserved historical evidence and unavailable-service coverage.","Check shared contracts, ownership, dependency ordering, release gates and rollback claims for contradictions across daemon, drivers and standalone packaging.","Check canonical artifact and live document alignment, citation support, missing implementation decisions and necessary visual evidence.","Use the originating ISSUE as upstream authority; do not invent HLD, DEF or future implementation-stage requirements."],"dependsOn":["daemon","drivers","native"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 26 inventory units map to substantive chunks. Shared contract, error, test and alternative sections are assigned across the implementation responsibilities they affect. Each assigned selector must be assessed in full, with responsibility-specific evidence retained. The final consistency chunk checks whole-artifact and originating ISSUE alignment without replacing substantive coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["daemon"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["daemon","drivers","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["native"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["daemon","drivers","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["daemon","drivers","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["drivers","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["daemon"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["native"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["drivers"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["native"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["native"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["daemon","native"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["drivers"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["drivers"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["native"]},{"unitId":"document:line:23","chunkIds":["daemon"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"daemon","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"drivers","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"native","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"dependabot-46667edf-design","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":7,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"daemon","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The design preserves the intended transport contracts and identifies relevant regression gates, but omits concrete daemon dependency selections and the originating issue’s unused-dependency removal work.","findings":[{"id":"daemon-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0/approach; LLD.md:119","message":"The chosen approach promises reviewed manifest ranges and parent-scoped constraints without specifying any daemon target versions, override entries, or advisory-to-package-path mapping. The cited lockfile contains the issue’s critical chain (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk 1.29.0 → express 5.2.1 → proxy-addr 2.0.7), but the design never states how that chain will change. Consequently, compatibility, complete advisory remediation, and npm override validity cannot be assessed before implementation. Add a concrete dependency decision table and proposed root-scoped override structure, including affected parent paths and compatibility rationale; record unresolved selections as open questions rather than leaving that list empty.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:115",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1.json#/body/openQuestions","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md — Root cause and Fix intent","package-lock.json:2843","package-lock.json:5502","package-lock.json:8194","[npm override semantics](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/package-json/#overrides)"]},{"id":"daemon-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/summary; /body/alternativesConsidered/0; /body/testStrategy","message":"The originating ISSUE explicitly includes removing unused dependencies after confirming callers in batch one. The LLD specifies neither removal candidates nor a caller-verification procedure or acceptance check for that work. Its CSV edge case mentions manifest cleanup, but never identifies the cleanup being authorized. For example, csv-parse remains a direct dependency while the inspected CSV execution path uses DuckDB read_csv_auto. Define the candidate inventory, require static and dynamic caller checks before removal, and map the resulting removals to regression coverage so this required scope cannot silently disappear.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md — Fix intent, batch (1)","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:61","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:78","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:119","package.json:52","src/daemon/db/file-execution.ts:45"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:23","/body/contractDetails","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-46667edffe5cc451.json","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md","package.json","package-lock.json — MCP SDK, Express, proxy-addr, undici, ws, Ollama, Zod, js-yaml and csv-parse entries","src/mcp/server.ts:1264","src/mcp/__tests__/mcp-process-e2e.test.ts","src/mcp/__tests__/schema-registry.test.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/http/index.ts — request redirects, cancellation, WebSocket lifecycle","src/agent/providers/ollama.ts:293","src/agent/providers/__tests__/ollama-private-transport.test.ts","src/daemon/db/file-execution.ts:45","https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/package-json/#overrides"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Name the existing MCP process and schema-registry suites in the transport qualification instructions: they already exercise real stdio-to-daemon forwarding and schema conversion.","No daemon interaction change or authored diagram is supplied. Existing transport code and the stated preservation contracts are sufficient for this responsibility; no diagram rendering was claimed or runtime qualification executed."]},{"chunkId":"drivers","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The design covers the intended integrations and separates ZIP runtime protection from tracker metadata, but batch-two dependency decisions and the security regression oracle need concrete specification.","findings":[{"id":"drivers-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails; /body/testStrategy","message":"Batch two names SMTP and four database integrations but supplies no dependency selections or compatibility decisions; contractDetails.api is empty. This leaves material choices unresolved: Cassandra 4.9.0 requires adm-zip ~0.5.10, while the cited extraction fix is in 0.6.1, outside that range. SQL Server actually uses tedious and tarn, and etcd carries gRPC dependencies. Specify the affected parent paths, proposed versions or scoped constraints, compatibility rationale, and corresponding transport/read checks. Include checks using existing saved connection configurations rather than only newly constructed SDK clients. Without these decisions, the second batch cannot be assessed as an implementable remediation preserving existing settings.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md — Fix intent, batch (2)",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1.json#/body/contractDetails","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:69","package-lock.json:4445","package-lock.json:5419","src/daemon/db/drivers/mssql.ts:7","src/daemon/db/drivers/cassandra.ts — registered factory","src/daemon/db/drivers/etcd.ts — registered factory","src/daemon/db/config.ts — loadConnections","[adm-zip 0.6.1 release](https://github.com/cthackers/adm-zip/releases/tag/v0.6.1)"]},{"id":"drivers-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/2; /body/testStrategy/testLevels/1","message":"The ZIP gate only names destination-symlink rejection, without specifying the exploit preconditions or an oracle distinguishing the fix from ordinary overwrite refusal. The advisory requires overwrite to be enabled; the currently installed vulnerable package defaults overwrite to false and can reject an existing target without exercising symlink protection. Specify overwrite=true, a benign archive entry targeting a pre-existing destination symlink to an outside sentinel, and assertions that outside content and permissions remain unchanged. Cover the affected synchronous, asynchronous and single-entry extraction APIs, or explicitly justify narrower coverage. Demonstrate that the fixture detects the vulnerable baseline before relying on it as the release gate.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:44","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:81","node_modules/adm-zip/adm-zip.js:671","node_modules/adm-zip/adm-zip.js:751","[Destination-symlink advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vwc7-r8mq-g2x9)","[Release documenting extraction protection](https://github.com/cthackers/adm-zip/releases/tag/v0.6.1)"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/8","/citations/9","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/dependabot-46667edf-design.json","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md","package.json","package-lock.json — SMTP, Cassandra, etcd, MySQL, tedious, tarn and adm-zip entries","src/daemon/tools/builtins/notify/index.ts:390","src/daemon/db/drivers/cassandra.ts","src/daemon/db/drivers/etcd.ts","src/daemon/db/drivers/mysql.ts — URL parsing and registered factories","src/daemon/db/drivers/mssql.ts — connection configuration, pool and factory","src/daemon/db/config.ts","src/daemon/db/file-execution.ts:45","src/daemon/db/__tests__/file-execution.test.ts","src/daemon/db/__tests__/mysql-integration.test.ts","src/daemon/db/__tests__/other-kv-probes.test.ts","src/daemon/db/__tests__/remaining-sql-probes.test.ts","src/indexer/target-resolution/config-sources.ts — Compose and Kubernetes parsers","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/inventory-kubernetes.ts — multi-document parsing and failures","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/inventory-ci.ts — YAML caller","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/inventory-docker.ts — YAML caller","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/inventory-helm.ts — YAML callers","src/analyze/explore/manifests-locate.ts — YAML caller","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/manifests-locate.test.ts — YAML cases","node_modules/adm-zip/adm-zip.js — extraction defaults","node_modules/cassandra-driver/lib/datastax/cloud/index.js — ZIP dependency usage","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vwc7-r8mq-g2x9","https://github.com/cthackers/adm-zip/releases/tag/v0.6.1"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Name the existing MySQL integration and Cassandra/etcd Docker probe suites in qualification instructions. The SQL Server probe suite mocks the SDK boundary, so it does not establish wire or TLS compatibility.","Clarify whether pending live checks block the affected batch or may be satisfied by specified fixtures. The ISSUE permits recording unavailable coverage, but the migration section does not define that release decision.","Scope multi-document YAML expectations to loadAll callers; Compose, CI and Helm use single-document load. Keep their existing parse-failure behavior explicit.","Citation c3 supports DuckDB CSV execution, while saved connection settings are supported by db/config.ts and the individual driver factories; add those references.","No interaction or UX changes require a new diagram for this responsibility. No visual verification or runtime qualification was claimed."]},{"chunkId":"native","status":"incomplete","summary":"The design correctly separates daemon embeddings from standalone caller-supplied vectors and requires independent consumer qualification. Two material gaps remain: concrete delivery of the narrowed SDK distribution and qualification of the promised rollback. The cited GitHub dashboard could not be inspected.","findings":[{"id":"native-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0/approach; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/4; LLD.md:119","message":"The selected remediation requires a reproducible narrowed LanceDB distribution, but does not define its upstream version and integrity source, derivation procedure, resulting package identity, delivery location, or dependency specification consumed by project-memory. These are central implementation decisions: the current package pins the ordinary 0.40.0 SDK, whose optional dependencies reinstall Transformers 3.0.2 and Sharp 0.33.5. Requiring checksum, license and native-target verification does not specify what artifact is being verified or how an independent installer obtains it. Define the immutable input, permitted manifest-only transformation, retained licensing/native dependencies, output identity and consumer delivery mechanism; identify associated manifest and packed-test changes. Record unresolved decisions in openQuestions instead of declaring none.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:119",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1.json#/body/openQuestions","packages/project-memory/package.json — dependencies and files","package-lock.json — node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb and its nested Transformers/Sharp entries","node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb/package.json — optionalDependencies, native targets and license","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/packed.test.ts:100","[npm package resolution rules](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/package-json/#overrides)"]},{"id":"native-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/migration/backwardCompat; /body/testStrategy; LLD.md:111","message":"Migration promises that reinstalling the previous package or daemon can reopen the same store, but qualification only names forward reopening of a pre-upgrade store. It does not require reopening with the previous release after the upgraded release has written data, nor provide a preserved-store recovery procedure if that reverse check fails. The cited packed tests create and reopen stores using the same installed artifact, so they do not establish either cross-release direction. Define the baseline artifact and populated fixture, assert preserved records/vectors and queue/receipt state after upgrade, and qualify old-version reopening after representative upgraded writes. Alternatively, constrain the rollback promise and specify a verified backup/restore procedure before deployment.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:85","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:111","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/packed.test.ts:129","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/packed.test.ts:141","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/fixtures/packed-store-consumer.mjs","packages/project-memory/src/store/lance-store.ts:184","packages/project-memory/src/store/format.ts — persistent format and embedding-profile validation"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/1","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-46667edffe5cc451.json","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md",".insrc/tmp/design-review/dependabot-46667edf-design.json — completed daemon and drivers feedback","package.json","package-lock.json — native SDK, Transformers, ONNX and Sharp dependency entries",".npmrc","packages/project-memory/package.json","packages/project-memory/src/types.ts — caller-owned ModelPort","packages/project-memory/src/model-dispatcher.ts — host embedding delegation","packages/project-memory/src/store/lance-store.ts — SDK loading, schema validation and store reopening","packages/project-memory/src/store/format.ts","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/packed.test.ts","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/fixtures/packed-store-consumer.mjs","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/fixtures/node22.ts","src/agent/providers/onnx-embedder.ts",".github/workflows/project-memory.yml","node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb/package.json","node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb/dist/index.js","node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb/dist/native.js — platform selection and binding version checks","node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb/dist/embedding/index.js","node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb/dist/embedding/openai.js","node_modules/@lancedb/lancedb/dist/embedding/transformers.js","docs/epics/share-project-memory-across-agents-applications-E2026110117123b6d/S003/evidence/t3-linux/project-memory-linux-node22-24a61e760b4e8e10787e91e658db362e1d6ab254/package-lock.json","docs/epics/share-project-memory-across-agents-applications-E2026110117123b6d/S003/evidence/t10-linux/project-memory-linux-node22-a4e040809abeaff4d966e79d6d1e4a639103654f/package-lock.json","docs/epics/share-project-memory-across-agents-applications-E2026110117123b6d/S003/evidence/t13-prewire-linux/project-memory-linux-node22-700c7f1e923a50717bbbf806105dc2b3d1bba98d/package-lock.json","docs/epics/share-project-memory-across-agents-applications-E2026110117123b6d/S003/evidence/t17-linux/project-memory-linux-node22-0990b423e1036ec1d2bf1783f20f40b62de77da3/package-lock.json","https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/package-json/#overrides"],"limitations":["/citations/10: The reference was assessed, but its GitHub Dependabot dashboard contents could not be verified. Browser retrieval failed and the read-only GitHub API attempt could not connect. The claimed alert inventory, eight low-alert exclusions and current tracker states therefore remain unverified against GitHub; originating ISSUE counts were treated as captured requirements."],"advice":["Make the native qualification matrix explicit by architecture and Linux libc. The existing workflow covers Linux, while the SDK declares macOS arm64 and several Linux targets; macOS coverage needs a separately identified execution environment.","Name the four archived lockfiles in reconciliation evidence and record their alert disposition separately. All four inspected files currently have SHA256 36845dda31bd234c0d174614c4995db2a199aae291e327f265a4093a9ee796cd and resolve Sharp 0.33.5.","The prose adequately explains caller-to-storage and SDK-to-binding ownership; a separate diagram is optional. No diagram definitions or rendered companions were supplied, and no visual verification is claimed.","Native installations, ONNX execution and cross-version store tests were not run during this read-only design review; they remain implementation release gates."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"The live LLD and canonical artifact agree and match the checkpoint baseline. The design preserves the main compatibility and qualification intentions, but does not explicitly retain the required three reviewable batches. Completed substantive feedback was inspected without duplicating its findings. GitHub alert inventory verification remains unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"consistency-001","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:72-109; /body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping; /body/migration","message":"The originating ISSUE requires three reviewable batches with targeted tests per batch and a full sweep afterward. The LLD lists tests by level and describes deployment steps, but never defines the three batch boundaries, their ordering, or their individual qualification checkpoints. Its ac1–ac4 labels also have no defined criteria in either the LLD or originating ISSUE. Consequently, the document does not establish how the required independently reviewable batches will be delivered and accepted. Explicitly map the three ISSUE batches to their scope and targeted qualification evidence, define the acceptance labels, and retain the final combined sweep. This is a design traceability requirement, not a request for future PLAN or TASKS artifacts.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md — Fix intent",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-46667edffe5cc451.json#/body/fixIntent","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:76","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:87","docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md:104"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/dependabot-46667edf-design.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-46667edffe5cc451-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/remediate-critical-high-moderate-dependabot-alerts-E2026110846667edf/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-46667edffe5cc451.json","Checkpoint completedChunks: daemon, drivers, native — all accepted completed feedback","Checkpoint baseline.reviewedContent — canonical and live document both match current files","packages/project-memory/package.json",".github/workflows/project-memory.yml","src/mcp/server.ts:1264","packages/project-memory/src/store/lance-store.ts:184","src/daemon/db/file-execution.ts:45","packages/project-memory/src/__tests__/packed.test.ts:100","src/agent/providers/onnx-embedder.ts:95","https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/package-json/#overrides","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vwc7-r8mq-g2x9","https://github.com/cthackers/adm-zip/releases/tag/v0.6.1"],"limitations":["LLD citation c11, https://github.com/insors-ai/insrc/security/dependabot, could not be retrieved: browser retrieval returned a cache-miss failure. The captured 122-alert inventory, eight low-alert exclusions, and current GitHub states could not be independently verified. This also preserves the unresolved verification limit reported by the native chunk."],"advice":["Retain daemon-001, daemon-002, drivers-001, drivers-002, native-001 and native-002 as the existing findings concerning dependency decisions, unused-dependency scope, ZIP regression validity, narrowed SDK delivery and rollback qualification; they are not repeated here.","Clarify the release treatment of unavailable live checks, as noted in drivers feedback: identify acceptable fixture evidence and which checks remain pending for the affected batch.","The ownership prose sufficiently distinguishes standalone caller-supplied vectors, the SDK-selected native binding and daemon-owned embeddings. No authored diagram or rendered companion is supplied; a separate diagram is optional, and no visual verification is claimed.","Native installs, service tests and store compatibility execution remain implementation qualification gates; they were not run during this read-only design review.","The distinction between ZIP runtime protection and advisory metadata is supported by the [advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vwc7-r8mq-g2x9) and [0.6.1 release notes](https://github.com/cthackers/adm-zip/releases/tag/v0.6.1)."]}],"limitations":["/citations/10: The reference was assessed, but its GitHub Dependabot dashboard contents could not be verified. Browser retrieval failed and the read-only GitHub API attempt could not connect. The claimed alert inventory, eight low-alert exclusions and current tracker states therefore remain unverified against GitHub; originating ISSUE counts were treated as captured requirements.","LLD citation c11, https://github.com/insors-ai/insrc/security/dependabot, could not be retrieved: browser retrieval returned a cache-miss failure. The captured 122-alert inventory, eight low-alert exclusions, and current GitHub states could not be independently verified. This also preserves the unresolved verification limit reported by the native chunk."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"30cc5f6b3fd95c0afaa21bb09c552470403df91e0bef2a1040e96c3e3ee72075"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-08T17:03:49.531Z"}],"applicableAttempt":1,"status":"incomplete","binding":{"sourceRevision":{"number":1,"contentHash":"aca29081dea457964e099ee84ed5f4533bb97eab337760ad96d62f382606ae8a"},"reviewedContentIdentity":"30cc5f6b3fd95c0afaa21bb09c552470403df91e0bef2a1040e96c3e3ee72075","documentDigest":"26ed0de8a4b41dbd56de73156f9d1eff1538164af2c3f96439431a4c15d972cd","workflowDigest":"387e5f3079f34282142381e6eaafb9873fcdf4adf9f46d9854fdfbbc5e890592","author":"controller"},"preservationDigest":"073e6d59167fa89eeed33ec05e1d62f821faaccdcaa0d7b7dbb287265a0577f6"}}}}
